      "findings": [
        {
          "source_quote": "καὶ οὕτω καθαροὶ σώματί τε καὶ ψυχῇ γενόμενοι τῆς ἐσομένης αἰδίου βασιλείας ἀπολαύσητε",
          "english_quote": "and then, having become clean in both body and soul, enjoy the eternal kingdom that is to come.",
          "issue": "“Then” conveys sequence but obscures the manner/result connection expressed by οὕτω and its contrast with the preceding οὐχ ἄλλως, “in no other way.” The more source-transparent “in this way” preserves that wording pattern without deciding that baptism alone, apart from the stated good deeds, causes cleansing.",
          "suggested_revision": "Replace this segment with “and in this way, having become clean in both body and soul, enjoy the eternal kingdom that is to come.” The replacement requires fresh review.",
          "severity": "minor"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "reference": "8.24",
